# CVE-2026-13506 — org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on (HIGH).
# Not exploitable here: Structural parse of keycloak/realm/realm-export.json: all 8 clients are
# protocol=openid-connect with clientAuthenticatorType=client-secret; zero SAML clients; only
# identityProvider is 'oidc' (Okta); registrationAllowed=false; sslRequired=external. The
# 'saml-role-list' mapper, 'saml ecp' flow, and 'client-x509' authenticator tier 1 cited are
# Keycloak's stock built-in realm defaults bound to no client, not live flows. Keycloak 26.7.2
# pom.xml pins FIPS BouncyCastle (bcfips 2.1.2 / bctls-fips 2.1.22) as its provider; the
# flagged bcprov-jdk18on-1.84.jar is a non-FIPS transitive artifact in the third-party base
# image. RedHat security data (access.redhat.com) rates the CVE Important but does not list Red
# Hat Build of Keycloak/RHSSO in package_state (only out-of-scope Fuse 7 / EAP 7).
# See: [TICKET]
CVE-2026-13506 exp:2026-12-22

