# CVE-2026-8763 — org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on (CRITICAL).
# Not exploitable here: bcprov-jdk18on-1.84.jar comes from the stock
# quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.2 base image (Dockerfile_keycloak:1); repo declares no
# BouncyCastle. The CVE's name-constraints validation path is exercised only during X.509 cert-
# chain validation (mTLS / client-cert auth). realm-export.json:887 sets tls-client-
# certificate-bound-access-tokens=false; no KC_HTTPS*, no truststore, no https-client-auth, and
# no .jks/.p12/.pem in docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile_keycloak, start.sh or the realm. The
# client-x509 authenticator (realm-export.json:2144) and SAML entries are Keycloak built-in
# defaults, not wired to an HTTPS+truststore flow. Federated login is OIDC to Okta via client
# secret (oidc-* mappers, KEYCLOAK_OKTA_IDP_CLIENT_SECRET), not certificate-based.
# See: UID2-7921
CVE-2026-8763 exp:2026-12-22

